.prop-exponent-gap"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.prop-exponent-gap"],"id":"long.prop-exponent-gap","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 2.9 (A bound for the reduced denominator)","locator":"Long record Proposition 2.9, p. 30, label prop:exponent-gap","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $n\\ge2$, let $\\mathrm{Skip}_n\\subseteq\\{2,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, and let $D_n$ be the reduced denominator of the associated finite sum. Since $D_n$ divides the product of its Mersenne denominators,\n$$\n\\log_2D_n\\le\\sum_{d\\in\\mathrm{Skip}_n}\\log_2(2^d-1)\n \\le\\sum_{d\\in\\mathrm{Skip}_n}d\\le\\frac{n(n-1)}2-1.\n$$\nThe middle inequality is strict when the skip set is nonempty; for an empty skip set both sums are zero. This is an upper bound, not a quadratic asymptotic for $D_n$. Combined with the cited fixed irrationality-measure exponent, it does not supply the required $2^{-3n/2}$-scale estimate. Even an asymptotic for the exponent sum would need additional information about the skip distribution.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.prop-exponent-gap","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.prop-exponent-gap","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.prop-exponent-gap%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.skipSum_den_dvd_prod%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.prop-exponent-gap%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.skipSum_den_dvd_prod%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.skipSum_den_dvd_prod"},{"derived":false,"family"